A Realpath system call for realpath(3): a system whose kernel resolves
paths whole, symbolic links and all, implements it and realpath asks it
in one call. mlibc's own walk, which stays for the other systems, does
not resolve the components of an absolute link's target or count the
links it follows, and reads each target into 512 bytes. Radix's kernel
returns the path its walk took (radix-directory(2)'s `real_path`).

